# HMAC-SHA-256 of each forbidden term (ADC-PRV-002), one per line, under a key
# that is not in the repository. Only the keyed hashes are committed, so the
# terms are not in the repository and cannot be found by hashing guesses.
#
#   python tools/forbidden_terms.py init-key       (once; the key stays outside the repository)
#   python tools/forbidden_terms.py add            (typed without being shown)
#   python tools/forbidden_terms.py scan-history   (every file and message of every commit)
#
# CI reads the key from the Actions secret ADC_TERMS_KEY. Where the key is not
# available, as on a fork, the scan is skipped and says so.
